n using AFLP markers as a means to assess the role of directional selection in the divergence of sympatric whitefish ecotypes</article-title><source>Mol Biol Evol</source><year>2004</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>945</fpage><lpage>956</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15014172</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/molbev/msh101</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rogers</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Bernatchez</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Genetic Architecture of Ecological Speciation and the Association with Signatures of Selection in Natural Lake Whitefish (<italic>Coregonus </italic>sp. Salmonidae) Species Pairs</article-title><source>Mol Biol Evol</source><year>2007</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>1423</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17404398</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/molbev/msm066</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rogers</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Bernatchez</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The genetic basis of intrinsic and extrinsic postzygotic isolation jointly promoting speciation in the lake whitefish species complex (<italic>Coregonus clupeaformis</italic>)</article-title><source>J Evol Biol</source><year>2006</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>1979</fpage><lpage>1994</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17040396</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1420-9101.2006.01150.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rise</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>von Schalburg</surname><given-names>KR</given-names></name><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>GD</given-names></name><name><surname>Mawer</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Devlin</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuipers</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Busby</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Beetz-Sargent</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Alberto</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Gibbs</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name><name><surname>Hunt</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Shukin</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Zeznik</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Nelson</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>SMR</given-names></name><name><surname>Smailus</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>SJM</given-names></name><name><surname>Schein</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Marra</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Butterfield</surname><given-names>YSN</given-names></name><name><surname>Stott</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Ng</surname><given-names>SHS</given-names></name><name><surname>Davidson</surname><given-names>WS</given-names></name><name><surname>Koop</surname><given-names>BF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Development and Application of a Salmonid EST Database and cDNA Microarray: Data Mining and Interspecific Hybridization Characteristics</article-title><source>Genome Research</source><year>2004</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>478</fpage><lpage>490</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14962987</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1101/gr.1687304</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>von Schalburg</surname><given-names>KR</given-names></name><name><surname>Rise</surname><given-names>ML<